  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRR-Team Kosovo 2023 &#x2013; Senior Flood Risk Expert</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In January, western and northern regions of Kosovo suffered from severe flash floods. This was the first time that these type of floods occurred. Due to ongoing heavy rainfall, rivers breached their banks. This left more than 20% of Kosovo&#x2019;s territory flooded, with severe damages estimated to amount over 20 million euros. The country is in an early recovery stage where the local situation is still urgent. The affected communities are located in the western and northern parts of the country, where the Kosovo Serbs, a minority, live. They are left with heavily damaged houses and loss of livelihoods while continuing to be at risk for future floodings. The lack of functioning infrastructure, i.e. muddy riverbanks, causes the rivers to overflow into their homes, which are built too close to the river side. The National government of Kosovo has requested technical support in riverbank management on prevention, mitigation, response and recovery.</narrative>
  </description>
